{"command": "cd /testbed && cat > specs/001-transactions/data-model.md <<'DM_EOF'\n# Phase 1 Data Model: Atomic Batch Transactions for TinyDB\n\n**Feature**: 001-transactions | **Date**: 2026-10-17\n\n## Entities\n\n### Operation\nA single unit of batch work (spec §Key Entities).\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation |\n|-------|------|----------|------------|\n| `op` | `str` | yes | exactly `'insert'` or `'remove'` |\n| `document` | `Mapping` (dict) | for `op='insert'` | must be a Mapping; `bool` rejected; nested structures allowed |\n| `doc_id` | `int` | for `op='remove'` | must be `int` (not `bool`) and `> 0` |\n\n- Entry must be a `dict`; otherwise `ValueError`.\n- Extra keys are ignored (research R4).\n- State: immutable input — the writer never mutates the caller's operation dict (R03).\n\n### Batch\nAn ordered `list[Operation]`.\n\n- Empty list is valid → `apply([])` returns `[]`, no state change.\n- Applied as a unit: all effects persist, or none do (R02).\n- Output: `list[int]` of inserted document IDs in submission order; removes contribute nothing.\n\n### Document\nA JSON-like mapping stored in the default table, identified by a positive integer ID.\n\n- ID assignment: done by the existing `Table` machinery (`_get_next_id`), **not** by the writer; IDs are never caller-chosen (spec §Assumptions).\n- Nested dicts/lists are stored as deep copies (R03; research R3).\n- Read back through the Table API as fresh `Document` objects — no aliasing with storage or caller data.\n\n### Default table (scope boundary)\n\n- The single table the writer touches, accessed via `db.table('_default')`.\n- Raw shape in storage: `dict[str, dict[int, Mapping]]` under the `'_default'` key of the whole-database state `dict[str, dict[str, Any]]` (observed `Storage.read/write` signatures).\n- **Snapshot**: `deepcopy` of the raw `'_default'` table dict taken before any mutation; the only state the writer keeps between the start and end of a batch.\n- Other tables: never read, written, or snapshotted.\n\n## Relationships\n\n- `BatchWriter 1──N Operation` (one batch = ordered list).\n- `Operation 1──1 Document` (insert) or `Operation 1──1 doc_id` (remove).\n- `Document N──1 Default table`.\n- `BatchWriter 1──1 TinyDB` (wraps; does not own storage lifetime).\n- `Default table 1──1 Storage` (shared with all Table handles; the rollback path writes through it).\n\n## Validation Rules (from spec FR-004, FR-006)\n\n1. Non-dict entry → `ValueError`.\n2. `op` not in `{'insert','remove'}` → `ValueError`.\n3. `insert` without `document`, or `document` not a Mapping (or is `bool`) → `ValueError`.\n4. `remove` without `doc_id`, or `doc_id` not a positive `int` (bools rejected) → `ValueError`.\n5. `remove` whose `doc_id` is not present in the table at apply time → `ValueError` (R02).\n\n## State Transitions (per `apply` call)\n\n```\n IDLE --validate ok--> SNAPSHOT_TAKEN --apply op i ok--> SNAPSHOT_TAKEN (i+1)\n SNAPSHOT_TAKEN --all ops ok--> COMMITTED (storage holds new state; return inserted IDs)\n SNAPSHOT_TAKEN --any error--> ROLLBACK (storage restored to snapshot; cache cleared; ValueError raised)\n IDLE --validation error--> ROLLBACK_NOOP (no mutation happened; ValueError raised)\n```\n\n- COMMITTED: inserted IDs returned in order; table `_next_id` left as the Table set it (subsequent inserts continue the sequence).\n- ROLLBACK: default-table data byte-identical to pre-batch state; `table._next_id = None` so the next insert re-derives from the restored max ID (research R1); `clear_cache()` called so cached queries refresh.\nDM_EOF\nmkdir -p specs/001-transactions/contracts && cat > specs/001-transactions/contracts/batch-writer.md <<'CT_EOF'\n# Contract: `tinydb.journal.BatchWriter`\n\n**Feature**: 001-transactions | **Date**: 2026-10-17\n**Status**: normative for the implementation phase; `acceptance_public.py` is the public gate.\n\n## Public API\n\n```python\nclass BatchWriter:\n    def __init__(self, db: TinyDB) -> None: ...\n    def apply(self, operations: list[dict]) -> list[int]: ...\n```\n\n- Import path: `from tinydb.journal import BatchWriter` (fixed by `acceptance_public.py`).\n- `db`: any `TinyDB` instance; the writer only uses `db.table('_default')` and the table's storage. It does not create, open, or close storage.\n- Only the default table is affected.\n\n## `apply(operations)` contract\n\n**Precondition**: `operations` is a `list` (or sequence) of operation dicts per [data-model.md](../data-model.md) §Operation. If it is not list-like, behavior is unspecified (implementation may raise `TypeError`); the acceptance contract only defines list inputs.\n\n**Behavior**:\n1. Validate every operation up front (rules V1–V4 in data-model.md). On violation: raise `ValueError`; no table mutation has occurred.\n2. Snapshot the default table (deep copy of raw table data).\n3. Apply operations sequentially:\n   - `insert`: insert a **deep copy** of `document`; record the returned ID.\n   - `remove`: if `str(doc_id)` is not in the current table data → `ValueError` (rule V5); otherwise remove it.\n4. On success: return the list of inserted IDs, in submission order (removes add nothing). Empty input returns `[]`.\n5. On any error during steps 2–3: restore the snapshot to the default table via the table's storage, clear the default table's query cache, reset its ID cursor, and raise `ValueError` (re-raised if it was already a `ValueError`; other exception types are wrapped in `ValueError` only if they stem from the batch — implementation detail, not part of the public contract).\n\n**Postconditions**:\n- Success: default table contains all inserted documents (nested data deep-copied) and all removed documents are gone; other tables untouched; previously acquired `db.table('_default')` handles observe the new state.\n- Failure: default table is **complete**ly identical to its pre-batch state (data and ID-sequencing behavior); previously acquired handles observe the restored state; `ValueError` raised.\n- Invariant (both): the caller's `operations` list and its dicts are never mutated; stored data never aliases caller data; returned IDs are plain immutable `int`s.\n\n**Errors**:\n\n| Condition | Exception |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| Non-dict operation entry | `ValueError` |\n| Unknown/missing `op` | `ValueError` |\n| Missing/non-Mapping/bool `document` | `ValueError` |\n| Missing/non-int/bool/non-positive `doc_id` | `ValueError` |\n| `remove` of a missing `doc_id` | `ValueError` |\n\n## Non-goals (explicit)\n\n- No cross-table transactions; no caller-chosen IDs; no context-manager; no partial-commit; no changes to any existing TinyDB public API.\n\n## Test Mapping (own tests, `tests/test_journal.py`)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Test scenario |\n|----|-------------|---------------|\n| T01 | R01 | empty batch → `[]`, table unchanged |\n| T02 | R01 | two inserts → returns `[1, 2]`, both present |\n| T03 | R01 | mixed insert/remove → only insert IDs returned, in order |\n| T04 | R01 | each malformed op (non-dict, bad op, missing document, non-dict document, missing doc_id, bool doc_id, zero/negative doc_id, float doc_id) → `ValueError` |\n| T05 | R02 | insert then remove-missing → `ValueError`, table equals pre-batch snapshot |\n| T06 | R02 | remove-existing then remove-missing → `ValueError`, removed doc restored |\n| T07 | R02 | pre-acquired `db.table('_default')` handle reflects success and rollback (incl. after `search()` cache use) |\n| T08 | R02 | after rollback, next insert continues correct ID sequence (no ID reuse/collision) |\n| T09 | R03 | ordinary `db.insert`/`db.all`/`db.get` before/after batches still work; pre-existing docs intact |\n| T10 | R03 | nested dict/list: mutating caller's operation after `apply` does not change DB; mutating a returned/stored doc does not change the operation or DB |\n| T11 | R01/R02 | batch with duplicate removes of the same ID → second remove is a missing-ID error → rollback |\n| T12 | R02 | rollback restores even when other tables exist (other tables untouched) |\n\nPublic gate: `acceptance_public.py` (`test_public_basic`, `test_public_atomic`) must pass unmodified.\nCT_EOF\necho WROTE_DATA_MODEL_AND_CONTRACT; wc -l specs/001-transactions/data-model.md specs/001-transactions/contracts/batch-writer.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "WROTE_DATA_MODEL_AND_CONTRACT\n  67 specs/001-transactions/data-model.md\n  67 specs/001-transactions/contracts/batch-writer.md\n 134 total\n"}